stranitsa-iz-dnevnika-name = diary page
stranitsa-iz-dnevnika-content = 15th day of Autumn Mists,

    {"Hut by the Black Backwater"}


    {"Settled."}

    {"If one can call by that word a gapped log hut roofed with moss, where the wind sings in the corners with all four elements, and by night the bogs sigh beneath the moon. But I am well here. From the threshold I can see Her castle - a dark silhouette on the neighboring marsh, the tower teeth catching low clouds, and one window still burning with her protective contour. I look at it every evening as I would look at a lighthouse. While it burns, she is there, beyond the veil, but not extinguished."}


    {"Longing is a strange beast. I thought that in eighty years I would grow used to waiting. But today she went especially deep into the astral, and the air around the tree grew dense, as before a storm. I sat among the roots, laid my palm upon the glowing bark, and kept silent. Words are not needed: she hears my silence as clearly as I hear her shimmering thread, stretching from timelessness into our world, thin but unbroken. My love, brightest shadow, I believe. I believe every word you spoke to Morbius, every step you take through the astral halls, where there is no time, but there is you."}


    {"Today I met the hunters. That is what the villagers call them here - crablike marsh giants that come out of the bogs in the season of mists. Before now they frightened people for nothing: overturning fishers' boats, breaking footbridges, hissing at night, sometimes even eating fishers in danger if those rushed at them with daggers! Superstitious folk barred doors and whispered charms. Yet it turned out they are simply curious. And lonely."}


    {"I went out to the backwater at sunset, when the shells crawled onto warm stones to bask. Three of them: a mother-matriarch with a shell streaked brown, and two smaller sons, though each was the size of a good boat. Their claws clicked uneasily, but their eyes - black and shining as jet - looked with reason. I raised empty hands: \"I am Goldur, a free mage-wizard. I shall live here by the backwater. I carry no evil, and ask the same of you toward people. Villagers are not your prey and not your sport.\" The matriarch looked through me for a long time, then clicked her claw twice - their gesture of agreement, as I later understood. A clatter like an oath."}


    {"We made an accord: the hunters do not trouble people, and I leave them part of the fish from the backwaters and share fire on cold nights, for marsh folk rarely receive dry warmth. The matriarch's sons brought me the ear of a vicious goblin as a gift - likely a delicacy to them. I hung it by my bed as a talisman of our pact. Now at night I hear not hissing, but measured clicking beyond the threshold - the hunters guard the backwater from strangers and look toward Keri's castle with me."}


    {"I will watch over her house while she prolongs her negotiations with eternity. I cannot live there now; everything reminds me of her... At least we had time to grow old together... Now I shall mend the contour, brush dust from the grimoires, light a candle in the library once each season, so magic remembers the warmth of human hands. And I will wait. A day, a year, a century - it matters not. My elemental magic is woven into the roots of this swamp now, and every leaf on our tree holds a particle of her voice."}


    {"If she stumbles in the astral, I will feel it. If she weeps, I will hear. If she tires, I will give her my strength through the tree that bound us more tightly than prayer and more tightly than death itself."}


    {"Come back, Keri. I am here. I am always here."}


    {"G. M."}

gryaznoe-pismo-name = dirty letter
gryaznoe-pismo-desc = A folded piece of rough paper, generously spattered with beer and something suspiciously like bird droppings. The handwriting is crude, the letters uneven and jumpy - apparently the village scribe barely kept up with the elder, carefully writing out every strong word.
gryaznoe-pismo-content = [color=#5c4033][head=2]Letter to Radomir[/head]


    {"Be well, neighbor Radomir. I write to you by chance carrier, for such things are happening here that saints would flee."}


    {"Remember I told you of the [bold]Rotten Bog[/bold]? There is no living with it now. Oversized crayfish have crawled out of there, [color=#8b0000]hunters[/color] they call them. Tall as a man, claws clacking, dogs in their bellies. And their chief is a brood-mother - [bolditalic]matriarch[/bolditalic], psia krew, big as a barn. The other day they dragged the miller into the mire, left only his boots."}


    {"The whole village pooled coin and hired a wanderer to rid us of the beast. One of those [color=#b8860b]mutants[/color]. Yellow eyes, two swords hanging on his back. That wretch haggled over every copper, [italic]curse his mother[/italic], as though we blew our noses with silver! Nearly shook the last trousers off us, the plague, ready to choke himself over each coin."}


    {"So he went to the swamp. In the morning he turns up - stinking of slime and guts, face covered in blood, dragging behind him on a rope the claw of that brood-mother, big as my cart. Threw it in the middle of the yard, swept our coin into his purse, glared with those [color=#b8860b]wolfish pale eyes[/color], and vanished without even saying farewell."}


    {"Rid us of her, he did, no argument. But now we will be eating goosefoot until autumn, because this savior cleaned us out to the last coin. [bold]Pah.[/bold] May we never see such benefactors again."}


    {"How is your harvest?[/color]"}

pylnoe-pismo-name = dusty letter
pylnoe-pismo-desc = Perfectly even, expensive parchment giving off a subtle scent of sandalwood and refined perfume. The lines are written in an elegant, sharp calligraphic hand, in which the writer's contempt is plainly visible.
pylnoe-pismo-content = [head=3]To the Esteemed Archmagister[/head]



    {"Greetings, Magister. My expedition to these distant holdings increasingly resembles an extended farce. If you believed peasant ignorance had any limits whatsoever, I must state: you were profoundly mistaken."}


    {"Yesterday I deigned to visit one of the coastal settlements in order to confiscate manuscripts whose discovery had been reported by our agents. And what happened? This toothless plebs answered me with categorical refusal! Imagine the degree of degradation: these unhewn barbarians claimed in all seriousness that the \"papers with strange squiggles\" belonged to their elder. When I reasonably asked about their use, it emerged that this ignoramus uses priceless scrolls containing formulas for sustaining the Barrier as kindling and for wrapping dried fish. What blatant profanation! My attempts to appeal to their reason and explain the sacred value of the artifacts shattered against a deaf wall of primitive obscurantism. They merely crossed themselves and spat over their shoulders."}


    {"Moreover, these serfs denied me elementary lodging. When, tired of fruitless discussion, I demanded a hot supper, I was told that \"this is no feeding house for witches\". In the end they tossed me a bowl of some stinking consistency, visually reminiscent of boiled rutabaga mixed with river silt. My discerning taste categorically rejected this vulgar substitute."}


    {"I urgently request that a proper expedition be dispatched for compulsory expropriation of the scrolls. My patience barely suffices to prevent me from turning this village into ash preemptively. I await your directives."}


    {"[bold]Ever yours,[/bold]"}

    {"[italic]Merlin Temnova[/italic]"}

razmytoe-poslanie-name = blurred message
razmytoe-poslanie-desc = A piece of thick parchment that clearly spent a long time in salt water. The edges are swollen and wavy, the surface covered with whitish crusts of dried sea salt. The scent of spices and campfire has almost completely faded, giving way to the sharp stink of rotten seaweed. Part of the text is washed away forever.
razmytoe-poslanie-content = [head=3]To respect...d batyr Kharzir from Kildibek[/head]


    {"Salam, dear br...ther Kharzir! Kildibek Ibn Nur-Ker...dy writes to you."}


    {"I heard your dzhigits somewhere ne... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...ring their sabres. People chatter, saying two great wolves in one forest will n... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...surely start gnawing each other's throats. Wai, what foo... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...people say this! Why should two honored warriors dull steel and spill blood?"}


    {"Listen here, dear one. I and my lads have taken one... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...under ourselves. A good village, fat! The peasants are timid as sheep, we sit in their huts like sultans... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] But these swineherds are cunning, I swear by my axe! They cry that they are poor, yet their main treasury is somewhere... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] They have sil...ver ringing there, and grivnas hidden away."}


    {"I say this to you: let us become sworn brothers, eh! Come to me with your lads as an ho... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...dear kunak. We shall slaughter the fattest ram, stir a cauldron of pilaf... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...and let wine flow like a river! We shall sit on carpets and speak as brothers."}


    {"We and your fellows will take these peasants by the legs and shake them well... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...they will give everything, nowhere to go. Silver - strictly half and half! Food, plunder - half... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] We shall live here together like khans, gathering tribute. Why should we wa... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color], when we can earn beautifully, yes?"}


    {"I await you, brother Kharz... Come with op... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color] ...and you will leave with a heavy purse!"}


    {"Your future... [color=turquoise]~~~[/color],"}

    {"Kildibek Ibn Nur-Ker...dy."}

cvernutyy-pergament-name = rolled parchment
cvernutyy-pergament-desc = A piece of thick parchment smelling faintly of pine needles and resin. The text is written in an elegant, flying hand, where some letters seem unusually rounded, like woven forest grasses.
cvernutyy-pergament-content = [head=3]Huntress Notes[/head]


    {"[italic]"}

    {"Third day of the moon."}


    {"Took the trail before dawn. The boar was fat, old. The arrow went under the shoulder blade like into butter. Skinned it myself. Brought the meat to the village, to the elder. They gave salt, groats, and a corner in the hayloft. People here are foolish, noisy, but not cruel. One can live. So long as they keep out of the forest."}


    {"Blood on the leaves."}


    {"Coyotes came. Cursed scoundrels. Bandits, with an orc for a chief, big as a hill. They burst into the square, women by the hair, men face-down in the dirt. The peasants only bleated like sheep. I loosed the bowstring three times. Three fell and did not rise. The elder shouted for me to leave. So I left by height: first onto the wall, then from it to the nearest oak."}


    {"Now I sit in an old shack. I hear them eating my meat and roaring with laughter. Let them enjoy it. They will not leave the village all the same. The forest is mine. And I still have two dozen arrows. We shall see how that orc sings when his dogs begin dying one by one in the bushes."}


    {"- Valira"}

    {"Barring"}

    {"[/italic]"}

obgorelyy-pergament-name = scorched parchment
obgorelyy-pergament-desc = A sheet of thick yellowish paper whose edges have turned to brittle coal. The surface is covered with soot and water stains, and the parchment itself gives off an acrid smell of burning. The text is written in a broad hand; in places the ink has run from drops of sweat or tears.
obgorelyy-pergament-content = [bold]Hear my words, beks and glorious bais of the neighboring lands![/bold]


    {"The elder of the hidden aul writes to you, from the village that has stood behind the Great Stone Wall since time immemorial. Oibai, great sorrow fell upon our heads last night!"}


    {"The sky was stained with a bloody glow when a giant fiery fox-shaitan emerged from the deep thicket. Nine tails lashed in the wind, burning all in their path! That kotakbas towered above our watchtowers and hid the moon. It roared so that the mountains shook, and its claws tore our stone fortifications as if they were thin wet felt."}


    {"Our finest dzhigits and most glorious batyrs did not shame their ancestors - with cries they rushed to defend the native hearth. Houses blazed, cauldrons melted, winter barns turned to grey ash before our eyes. We were already saying farewell to our lives."}


    {"But then our high shaman stepped onto the wall. May the spirits receive him with honors! He did not flinch before the nine-tailed bastard. Calling to the very bowels of the mountain, he wrought ancient and mighty earth magic. Huge stone blocks rose from the soil, binding the beast's paws and maw, and the shaman gave his own flesh and blood to imprison the demon's essence forever in the body of a newborn orphan."}


    {"[color=#333333]██▓▒░[/color]"}

    {"[bold]Damage to our kin:[/bold]"}

    {"[color=#555555]- Half the yurts and stone houses reduced to dust.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]- Winter stores of grain and dried meat burned to nothing.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]- Main gate of hundred-year oak burned through completely.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]- [color=#8b0000]▒░█[/color] dzhigits slain, the rest need salves for burns.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]- Livestock scattered across the steppe in panic.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#333333]░▒▓██[/color]"}


    {"We need healers, strong logs, and carts of kumis to raise the spirits of the survivors. We shall not let our aul be wronged, and the boy with the demon inside him is now under our watch. The shaman has fallen, but the earth still remembers his strength."}

zalyapannyy-pergament-name = stained parchment
zalyapannyy-pergament-desc = A single sheet of thick paper with charred edges. It reeks unbearably of sour ale, malt, and singed wool. The parchment is badly warped by moisture, and the broad, twitching handwriting has blurred in places.
zalyapannyy-pergament-content = [color=#3b2f2f]Wai-dod... I am alive, plague take me! Alive! But better if I died there in the cave!


    {"And all because of my greed, psia krew! Wise folk said: 'Do not go to the mountain, you will burn like dry dung!' But I was very clever. Thought the lizard slept, I would fill a sack with gold and become a great bai! Crept in quiet-quiet, dark all around, stinking of sulfur. I had just snatched one golden cup - and it, curse it, caught another and [italic]rang[/italic]! The eye opened at once. Huge, yellow, like sour kumis. I dropped the sack and ran, but where can one run on my crooked legs..."}


    {"Listen further, dzhigit. This [bold][color=#8b0000]Red Mascot[/color][/bold] pinned me in the corner. Sent flame - not to kill, yes, but to frighten! Singed my backside so badly I shall lie only on my belly for a week, by my beard! My trousers behind burned ░░░░░ all the way to the knees!"}


    {"I sit shaking like a sheep before slaughter. Waiting for it to start chewing. And this scaly shaitan sticks its huge muzzle right in my face. I squeezed my eyes shut, yes... And then I smell it - wai, Mother of God! It does not stink of sulfur! It reeks of hangover! Like an old tavernkeeper on Sunday morning, psia krew!"}


    {"And it speaks to me in a voice that made my ears ring:"}

    {"[italic][color=#8b0000]\"Listen here, thief... You owe me your life now.\"[/color][/italic]"}


    {"I thought it would take my soul, or make me clean its boots with my tongue! But it... ▓▓▓▓▒▒▒ it says:"}

    {"[italic][color=#8b0000]\"Two kegs of [color=#d4af37]dark[/color]. Every week. Drag them straight here. With a thick head of foam, kurva, or I will snack on you.\"[/color][/italic]"}


    {"A beer dragon! Have you ever seen such a thing?! Fairy tales all lie, clever city folk! What Terror of the Mountains? He is a winged drunkard!"}


    {"Now my back hurts like an old donkey's. Drag two kegs up the mountain! Where am I to get that much tenge for good drink?! I will have to ask the tavernkeeper for debt, or water it down... Though no, water is bad, he will burn me to hell!"}


    {"Wallahi, had I known, I would rather have pitched dung with a fork. Every week... Two kegs... Wai-dod, why this sorrow upon me?! Save my soul... and my lower back.[/color]"}

pomyataya-zapiska-name = crumpled note
pomyataya-zapiska-desc = A rough piece of dense grey paper. The sheet is thickly covered with ingrained coal dust, and greasy fingerprints and a few drops of dried blood show along the edges.
pomyataya-zapiska-content = [head=2]ORDER[/head]


    {"Listen here, you wretches! The old gallery on the lower tier collapsed to the dogs. [color=#4a4a4a]▓▓▓[/color] I told that pockmarked fool to set double supports, but he must have been counting crows!"}


    {"So carve this onto your noses: until I personally inspect every stone down there, no one sets foot in it. The ceiling is currently held up by spit and someone's mother. If I see anyone head into the fall after a dropped pick or shiny ore, I will lay the haft across his back so hard he will not sit for a week. [color=#2b2b2b]▒▒▒[/color] Goblins take you, I need no corpses under collapses here."}


    {"And one more thing. I hid a small keg of good ale behind the old smelter. Whoever touches it before the end of the shift will eat raw ore for supper."}


    {"Now move and swing those picks, layabouts! The quota will not fill itself!"}

gryaznyy-pergament2-name = dirty parchment
gryaznyy-pergament2-desc = A crumpled sheet of cheap paper smeared with mud. The letters are large and uneven, clearly written by a barely literate man, and the parchment itself distinctly reeks of manure.
gryaznyy-pergament2-content = [head=2]Complaint[/head]

    {"Good Elder, sir! Vladek from the far yard writes to you. "}

    {"My neighbor, Zhdan, has gone clean mad. The other day he traded with a traveling merchant for some shiny nonsense, says it is an amulet against goblins. And now this... [color=#4a4a4a]▓▓▓[/color] Zhdan, meaning, walks around my pigsty at night and mutters like those half-wits in skirts from the Collegium. "}

    {"And today my best sow, Ryabaya, farrowed. And what do you think? One piglet is the very image of Zhdan! Just as bald, and squeals just as foully. [color=#8b4513]▒▒▒[/color]"}

    {"I demand that you have Zhdan flogged, or at least make him pay me damages in copper for spoiling my pig. Otherwise I will break his head with a cart shaft myself, by God. "}

    {"Written by my own hand, Vladek."}

